Greetings,
  I have found what may be a bug in Nethack 3.0 pl 7, downloaded
from uunet fully patched.  I'm running on AT&T 3B2 (Somethings - I
know they're big), SYSTEM V R 3.2.1.  Anyway, when I use a wand (so
far ANY wand), instead of seeing a bolt of fire or whatever, I see:

---------------
|@-50-50-50-50| when firing to the right, and various other messy
|.............|
|.............|
---------------

variations when firing diagonally.  It appears that after printing
the bolt character, '-', '/', '\', or what have you, '50' is appended.
This also happens when I get large black knives thrown at me by
those monsters I can't remember the name of right now.  (I've only
had it for a day so far, forgive me)  Dragon fire did the same thing
only I noticed many '*' in there too.

  I made a quick look through zap.c hoping I might see something
to fix, but I didn't.  Also, I'm not too sure that this is a bug or a
quirk with the 3B2.  I haven't seen mention of it posted yet, and
it's pretty obvious.  The compilation went well. I used the
STUPID_CPP (?) option to get rid of the 'too many defines' errors,
and otherwise, all the options were included.  No problems - the
binary worked the first time.
  
Thanks for any help you might be able to give me.  Also, many thanks
